imum subarray sum within a single instance of `values`.\n    max_sum = _kadane(values)\n\n    # If k is 1, the problem is a standard Kadane's algorithm.\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum\n\n    # For k > 1, we need to consider sums that span across multiple repetitions.\n\n    # 2. Calculate the total sum of `values`.\n    total_sum = sum(values)\n\n    # 3. Calculate the maximum prefix sum of `values`.\n    # This is the maximum sum ending at any index from the start.\n    max_prefix = values[0]\n    current_prefix_sum = values[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_prefix_sum += values[i]\n        max_prefix = max(max_prefix, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    # 4. Calculate the maximum suffix sum of `values`.\n    # This is the maximum sum starting at any index from the end.\n    max_suffix = values[n - 1]\n    current_suffix_sum = values[n - 1]\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        current_suffix_sum += values[i]\n        max_suffix = max(max_suffix, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # 5. Consider subarrays that span across two instances of `values`.\n    # This would be a maximum suffix from the first array combined with a maximum prefix from the second.\n    max_sum_two_arrays = max_prefix + max_suffix\n    max_sum = max(max_sum, max_sum_two_arrays)\n\n    # 6. If k > 2 and the total sum of `values` is positive, we can include full blocks\n    # in between the first and last parts of the subarray.\n    if k > 2 and total_sum > 0:\n        max_sum_with_middle_blocks = max_sum_two_arrays + (k - 2) * total_sum\n        max_sum = max(max_sum, max_sum_with_middle_blocks)\n\n    return max_sum", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/293": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/293", "solution": "import math\ndef otherside_rightangle(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the third side (hypotenuse) of a right-angled triangle\n    given the lengths of the other two sides.\n    \"\"\"\n    return math.sqrt(a**2